# Git and commits

- Messages: short, imperative, factual — e.g. `fix(vms): curl -4 for IPv6-broken hosts`
- No trailing summaries in the commit body unless the user asks
- **Never** add `Co-Authored-By: Claude`, `Co-Authored-By: Cursor`, or any AI attribution
- Never commit `CLAUDE.md`, `.DS_Store`, `secrets.yaml`, or credential files
- Only commit when the user explicitly asks
- No force-push / hard reset / amend unless the user explicitly requests it
- Never mention kcli in commits, docs, code, or comments

Credentials live in `~/.rodeo/secrets.yaml` (chmod 600). Plans use `??key`. Never put real credentials in the repo.
